##############################
# Secrets & credentials
##############################
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.env
..env.*
.env
.env*
# …but TEMPLATES must ship: they carry placeholders only, never real credentials.
# Users copy `.envN.example` → `.env` and fill in their own secrets. Without these
# negations the `.env*` rule above silently swallows them and they never reach GitHub.
!.env.example
!.env1.example
!.env2.example
!.env3.example
# Plaintext credential exports from the admin console / bulk provisioning.
# These contain real usernames + passwords — never commit them.
user_credentials*.csv
credentials*.csv
gitpat.txt
my_password.txt
**/id_rsa
**/id_rsa.pub
**/id_ed25519
**/id_ed25519.pub
**/known_hosts
